mapping "W4613.1" source="W4613" target="821431000000102" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W4613 SNOMED CT 821431000000102 = Swedish national extension of ICD-10 W46 (Contact with
        hypodermic needle) further specified by place (institutional residence, Y92.x) and activity
        (other specified activity, Y93.x). The injury event itself is identical to W46. Target SNOMED CT
        44806406 (standard_concept=S, domain=Condition, class=Disorder) is the canonical injury concept
        for hypodermic-needle contact; it does not encode place/activity, which in OMOP are recorded as
        separate context axes (visit/observation), not in the condition concept. The ICD10CM mirror
        confirms the equivalence: every W46.x subcode (W46.0XXA, W46.1XXD, etc., including all
        place+activity variants) carries an Athena edge to 44806406. Mapping_type broader because the
        target fully subsumes the clinical injury meaning while the dropped place/activity is
        administrative context, not a separate clinical concept. Confidence : small, well-understood
        breadth mismatch with verified crosswalk via the ICD10CM equivalent.
        """
}
mapping "W4614.1" source="W4614" target="821431000000102" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source W4614 SNOMED CT 821431000000102 = Swedish extension of W46 (Contact with hypodermic needle)
        at institutional residence during vital activity (rest/sleep/meal/personal hygiene). Injury
        event identical to W46; target SNOMED CT 44806406 (S, Condition, Disorder) is the canonical injury
        concept, dropping place (Y92) and activity (Y93) context. ICD10CM mirror confirms all W46.x
        subcodes SNOMED CT 821431000000102 44806406. Mapping_type broader: target subsumes the clinical
        injury; dropped context is administrative. Confidence : verified crosswalk, small
        well-understood breadth mismatch.
        """
}
